gt;The Seattle city government provides a public API for fire department emergency dispatch data. There’s a very cool project, &lt;a href=&#34;https://sfdlive.com&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;SFD Live&lt;/a&gt;, that visualizes this information (and a lot more) with a ton of features.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;What I wanted, though, was something much simpler: a stripped-down view of the data that would be interesting, if not especially useful, on a dashboard I could glance at from across the room. I had an old monitor and a spare Raspberry Pi lying around, so slapping those together and running a web app in kiosk mode on the Pi felt like the perfect excuse for a small side project.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
